#
# Counter-example for math:ModelFormulaSlotExpressionConstraint: a math:ModelFormula
# whose math:ArgumentSlot carries its index but NO math:slotExpression. The R lift
# renders a model formula as a binder over INDEXED operand slots precisely so the
# response, terms, interactions and offsets are inspectable structure; a slot with an
# index and no expression is a formula the lift could not structure, which is the
# graph-side residue of the front-end's math:UnliftableRComputation refusal.
#
# The formula is well-formed everywhere else, so the violation stays minimal: it carries
# the one math:argumentSlot its own min-1 frame requires (so it is not
# math:UnframedFunction), the slot carries a single xsd:integer math:slotIndex within
# math:ArgumentSlot's max-1 frame (so it is not math:MalformedArgumentSlot), and no part
# of the expression is represented by a bare string literal. The obligation is about the
# SLOT rather than the formula's own cardinality, so it has no OWL antecedent to lean on
# and is authored as a logic:Constraint. It fires
# math:ModelFormulaSlotExpressionConstraint (shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent →
# math:UnliftableRComputation).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/model-formula-slot-no-expression/> .

ex:formula a math:ModelFormula ;
    math:argumentSlot ex:slot0 .

# Indexed, and empty: the ~ binder's slot is present with nothing bound into it.
ex:slot0 a math:ArgumentSlot ;
    math:slotIndex "0"^^xsd:integer .
